<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> was a short-lived state proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a> in October 1918 by the South Slav lands leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>. Governed by a national council, it united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, Croatia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>. On 1 December 1918 it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> to form the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/state-of-slovenes-croats-and-serbs.jpg" alt="State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orlovic: I drew this flag in photoshop, on the base of another version on the internet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Slovenes,_Croats_and_Serbs.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
